Status: UNTESTED. Not compiled: the LLVM build tree does not fit on the
orb. Applies to mbrock/fil-c d6cbb697f74c (lib/filc-upstream.json coreRev)
with `patch -p1` in a fil-c checkout.

What is verified: the slowdown reproduces with the pinned compiler, and
gdb samples of a slow compile are all in the loop this patch replaces
(unordered_map<ValuePtr, FrameEntry> lookups called from
Pizlonator::computeFrameIndexMap).

Reproducer: one function with N pointers live at once.

    #include <stdlib.h>
    void sink(void *);
    void f(void) {
      void *p0 = malloc(1); ... void *pN = malloc(N+1);
      sink(p0); ... sink(pN);
    }

    clang -O1 -c: N=500 1.0 s, N=1000 4.3 s, N=2000 41 s
    clang -O0 -c, N=2000: over 5 minutes and 2.8 GB

Asio 1.36's unit/execution/any_executor.cpp compiles in 10 s at -O0 and
took over an hour at -O2 in the asio check (5.7 GB RSS).

The greedy frame-slot coloring tried each index against every
neighbor with a hash lookup each time, O(V * colors * degree), cubic
for dense interference. Collect the indices of already-placed neighbors
once per value and take the lowest free one: O(E) overall, with the
same assignment (the same lowest free index in the same order).

